# WRAP + QUIZZES
add('Question 1 · unsupervised or supervised?',quiz(1,'Which statement describes PCA?', ['It chooses axes with the highest separation of disease labels.','It chooses directions retaining maximal sample variance.','It assigns each patient a verified disease subtype.']))
add('Question 2 · preprocessing',quiz(2,'Why could unscaled PCA be misleading for hemoglobin, weight and age?', ['Scaling never changes principal components.','PCA is invariant to units and variance.','The variable with greater numerical variance can dominate the projected directions.']))
add('Question 3 · interpreting clusters',quiz(3,'Which conclusion is justified after K-means identifies three clusters of metabolomic profiles?', ['The three clusters are different Alzheimer’s subtypes.','The chosen algorithm found three groups under its assumptions; biological meaning needs validation.','The algorithm has therefore demonstrated treatment causality.']))
add('Question 4 · evaluation',quiz(4,'What is a defensible use of the final test set?', ['Evaluate a fully chosen pipeline once at the end.','Use it repeatedly to choose model depth and features.','Fit preprocessing on all patients before splitting.']))
add('Question 5 · generalization',quiz(5,'A deep decision tree has nearly zero training error but high validation error. What is most plausible?', ['It must be unbiased in future patients.','It cannot classify any observations.','It has probably overfit incidental training patterns.']))
add('Question 6 · real-world interpretation',quiz(6,'A model recognizes handwritten digits with high accuracy on a held-out dataset. Which claim follows?', ['It will necessarily diagnose disease with equal accuracy.','It has demonstrated prediction on its tested digit data, not clinical validity.','Its predictions prove which pixels cause the digit to be what it is.']))
add('One intellectual framework, twelve weeks',flow([('Probability','Describe uncertainty'),('Inference','Estimate from samples'),('Modeling','Relate variables appropriately'),('Prediction','Generalize to unseen data')]),'<div class="w12-hero" style="font-size:.82em;margin:.75em auto;">The same principles persist as models grow more complex.</div>')
add('Statistics is not superseded by AI',cards([('observed','Data','Who was sampled? What was measured? Can we trust labels?'),('uncertainty','Inference','What assumptions, variability and uncertainty remain?'),('warning','Bias','What confounding, leakage, selection and distribution shift might mislead us?'),('estimate','Generalization','Does the claim survive independent evaluation and domain scrutiny?')]))
add('The final course takeaway',eyebrow('Statistics 101 · Graduate Pharmaceutical Studies'),'<div class="w12-quote">Good statistical thinking means knowing <strong>what the evidence supports, what remains uncertain, and when a confident model can still be wrong.</strong></div>','<div class="w12-hero">The goal was never to memorize a list of tests. <strong>It was to reason about scientific evidence.</strong></div>',cls='title-slide')

